WEBVTT

00:00:18.967 --> 00:00:20.533
Out of the way! You can't handle it!

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:48.500
"My-HiME"

00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:52.733
<i>All across the blue sky</i>

00:00:52.733 --> 00:00:56.100
<i>our feelings</i>

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:59.833
<i>are being mounted like gems</i>

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:04.400
<i>If only you were</i>

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.767
<i>my soul mate</i>

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:14.433
<i>but reality doesn't work that way</i>

00:01:14.433 --> 00:01:19.567
<i>In the sparkling wind</i>

00:01:19.567 --> 00:01:26.967
<i>the wings of dreams descend</i>

00:01:26.967 --> 00:01:30.567
<i>Gather the courage to go into the future</i>

00:01:30.567 --> 00:01:35.400
<i>with beauty</i>

00:01:37.467 --> 00:01:42.867
<i>The hot heartbeats begin to pulse</i>

00:01:42.867 --> 00:01:46.333
<i>at the same speed</i>

00:01:46.333 --> 00:01:50.000
<i>I felt that day</i>

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:55.933
<i>I like direct gazes</i>

00:01:55.933 --> 00:02:03.700
<i>I want to stare forever</i>

00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:14.067
"Dance of Flames / Star's Oath"

00:02:31.433 --> 00:02:32.967
That girl...

00:02:32.967 --> 00:02:34.100
Hey!

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:48.733
It's not hot.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:51.867
What is this?

00:02:51.867 --> 00:02:54.067
Calm down, Mai.

00:02:55.633 --> 00:02:59.600
That's the Element.
Proof you have the power of a HiME.

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:00.367
Nagi!

00:03:00.367 --> 00:03:02.467
It's that guy...

00:03:07.833 --> 00:03:09.067
Takumi!

00:03:10.867 --> 00:03:12.833
I wasn't expecting that one.

00:03:12.833 --> 00:03:15.333
Pretty impressive for a first timer.

00:03:29.767 --> 00:03:31.333
Miroku!

00:04:06.533 --> 00:04:07.900
Mai!

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:09.067
Mikoto...

00:04:09.067 --> 00:04:11.467
I had no idea you were a HiME!

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:14.067
I think this is...

00:04:14.067 --> 00:04:15.500
...a misunderstanding...

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:18.500
Oh! You call that Misunderstanding, huh?

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:19.733
This is Miroku!

00:04:19.733 --> 00:04:21.667
Uh, that's not what I meant.

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:22.900
You two!

00:04:24.567 --> 00:04:26.533
This is as far as you're gonna go!

00:04:26.533 --> 00:04:28.433
I told you not to get involved!

00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:31.100
Don't do it!

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:33.067
She's right.

00:04:33.067 --> 00:04:36.067
I think you two are jumping the gun.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:53.800
Duran!

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:55.933
Load Chrome Cartridge!

00:04:58.433 --> 00:04:59.600
Fire!

00:05:02.833 --> 00:05:04.400
It's relentless!

00:05:28.867 --> 00:05:31.733
Why me? What's happening?

00:05:31.733 --> 00:05:33.700
Sis...

00:05:39.867 --> 00:05:41.933
But...

00:05:41.933 --> 00:05:43.900
I promised to look after you...

00:05:47.567 --> 00:05:49.733
All right, monster...

00:05:56.800 --> 00:05:58.800
I made a promise!

00:06:10.067 --> 00:06:11.367
Takumi!

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:21.933
Mai, look behind you.

00:06:25.467 --> 00:06:26.600
What?

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:31.967
I'll let you in on a secret.
He was here protecting you all along.

00:06:31.967 --> 00:06:33.833
Kagutsuchi.

00:06:33.833 --> 00:06:38.033
Who would've figured
that he was your Child?

00:06:38.033 --> 00:06:40.767
That's right! I know!

00:07:02.633 --> 00:07:03.800
That day...

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:06.867
That's right. A Child is
the guardian angel of a HiME.

00:07:06.867 --> 00:07:10.367
Now you must decide
whether you will accept him.

00:07:10.367 --> 00:07:13.433
Will you accept Kagutsuchi
and fight with him or not?

00:07:13.433 --> 00:07:14.667
Mai...

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:16.033
No, Mai-HiME...

00:07:16.033 --> 00:07:17.500
Stop it!

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:18.567
Whoa...

00:07:18.567 --> 00:07:20.667
Don't let him talk you into anything!

00:07:25.833 --> 00:07:29.033
Well, you probably don't
need me to tell you this,

00:07:29.033 --> 00:07:30.433
but if you choose to fight,

00:07:30.433 --> 00:07:34.367
you'll have to risk the one thing
that's most important to you.

00:07:37.867 --> 00:07:40.800
You mean I'll have to risk my life...

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:43.367
I'll be more than glad to!

00:07:43.367 --> 00:07:44.967
I figured you would, Mai-HiME!

00:07:44.967 --> 00:07:46.833
Now remove the sealed sword.

00:07:46.833 --> 00:07:47.833
No!

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:55.367
Kagutsuchi!

00:07:58.433 --> 00:07:59.733
The fool!

00:08:24.667 --> 00:08:26.000
What is this?!

00:08:37.767 --> 00:08:39.533
Kagutsuchi...

00:09:07.333 --> 00:09:08.900
Duran!

00:09:14.833 --> 00:09:16.767
Wh-What's going on?!

00:09:22.367 --> 00:09:25.500
What?! What are you
going to do, Kagutsuchi?!

00:09:29.033 --> 00:09:30.767
Mikoto! Natsuki!

00:09:30.767 --> 00:09:32.633
Run!

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:11.333
Damn...

00:10:15.067 --> 00:10:17.533
Big Sis...

00:10:17.533 --> 00:10:19.667
Takumi...

00:10:20.667 --> 00:10:22.433
Mai!

00:10:22.433 --> 00:10:23.500
Incredible!

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:25.633
You're really strong, Mai!

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:28.933
You...

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:32.433
Mai!

00:10:32.433 --> 00:10:34.567
Come on! Mai!

00:10:34.567 --> 00:10:35.800
Mai!

00:10:43.067 --> 00:10:44.700
Mai...

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:48.467
Please take care of Takumi.

00:11:12.867 --> 00:11:16.900
His breathing is stable. He'll be just fine.

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:19.633
Last night must've been too much for him.

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:25.933
Sis.

00:11:25.933 --> 00:11:27.600
I-I...

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:29.000
Takumi!

00:11:30.333 --> 00:11:32.867
--Takumi!
--H-Hey, Sis!

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:37.433
First the lawn, and now the back hill.

00:11:37.433 --> 00:11:40.600
There won't be any shortage of rumors.

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:41.533
A wildfire?

00:11:41.533 --> 00:11:43.633
It wouldn't get that out of hand.

00:11:43.633 --> 00:11:44.933
You think?

00:11:44.933 --> 00:11:47.500
It's where a UFO landed.

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:48.733
You can't be serious.

00:11:48.733 --> 00:11:50.900
I heard Suzushiro of the Executive
Committee has gone ballistic,

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:53.900
and that she's demanding a full inquiry!

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:57.000
Someone should find her a boyfriend.

00:12:01.933 --> 00:12:02.967
Jeez.

00:12:02.967 --> 00:12:07.533
Who's the idiot that messed up my picture?

00:12:09.667 --> 00:12:10.867
This girl, right?

00:12:10.867 --> 00:12:12.733
Got it?

00:12:12.733 --> 00:12:14.367
Thought so.

00:12:14.367 --> 00:12:17.767
Figures she came here
on a Kazahana scholarship.

00:12:17.767 --> 00:12:20.000
How come you're so
interested in her all of a sudden?

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:23.333
No reason.

00:12:23.333 --> 00:12:26.433
Does this have something to do
with what happened on the back hill?

00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:34.800
Sorry, Shizuru. I just don't want
you to get wrapped up in this.

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:37.033
That's so cute of you to say.

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:41.067
Good-bye, Kanzaki.

00:12:41.067 --> 00:12:43.333
Careful on your way home.

00:12:43.333 --> 00:12:45.533
Okay!

00:12:45.533 --> 00:12:46.933
So, Kanzaki...

00:12:46.933 --> 00:12:49.567
...what are we going to do
about the Founders' Day Festival?

00:12:49.567 --> 00:12:51.800
Well, with all that's happened,

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:54.367
we can't go through
with the boat party plan.

00:12:54.367 --> 00:12:56.533
We'll have to start over.

00:12:56.533 --> 00:13:00.533
Well, I wasn't in a hurry to
get back on a boat any time soon.

00:13:01.767 --> 00:13:05.033
From now on I'll be sure to
send you somewhere a lot safer.

00:13:05.033 --> 00:13:08.933
Somehow that doesn't seem very reassuring.

00:13:11.967 --> 00:13:14.033
Natsuki Kuga.

00:13:14.033 --> 00:13:17.333
Oh? Not interrupting, are we?

00:13:17.333 --> 00:13:19.967
You sure are. Right at the juicy part.

00:13:19.967 --> 00:13:22.033
Shizuru!

00:13:22.033 --> 00:13:23.867
I was kidding, take it easy.

00:13:23.867 --> 00:13:26.867
I've got an idea. How about some tea?

00:13:26.867 --> 00:13:29.067
Wasn't there a good mandarin tea around?

00:13:29.067 --> 00:13:31.067
You want me to get it?

00:13:31.067 --> 00:13:32.600
I'm leaving.

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:34.367
Oh, come on.

00:13:34.367 --> 00:13:37.433
Why don't you relax and stay a while?

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:43.067
Student Council room.

00:13:43.067 --> 00:13:44.100
Yes?

00:13:44.100 --> 00:13:45.933
The Headmaster?

00:13:50.967 --> 00:13:53.433
You're okay now.

00:13:53.433 --> 00:13:58.733
What made you push yourself
to the point of having seizures?

00:14:02.067 --> 00:14:06.633
Don't tell me it had something
to do with that incident last night.

00:14:06.633 --> 00:14:08.867
Um, well...

00:14:11.567 --> 00:14:13.800
Actually, I don't really remember

00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:15.467
anything that happened last night.

00:14:15.467 --> 00:14:18.633
What?! You don't remember?!

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:21.833
Mai?

00:14:21.833 --> 00:14:23.800
Excuse me.

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:25.467
Oh, there she is.

00:14:25.467 --> 00:14:30.033
The Headmaster has asked me
to bring you to her, Tokiha.

00:14:30.033 --> 00:14:31.633
Me?

00:14:31.633 --> 00:14:34.400
She sent us to get you.
She wants to talk.

00:14:34.400 --> 00:14:34.967
But...

00:14:34.967 --> 00:14:36.500
Oh, yes.

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:40.400
The school has officially announced
what happened on the back hill.

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:41.833
It was a lightning strike.

00:14:41.833 --> 00:14:42.733
What?!

00:14:42.733 --> 00:14:44.033
Were you listening in?

00:14:44.033 --> 00:14:45.433
To what?

00:14:45.433 --> 00:14:47.767
You're a hard nut to crack, aren't you?

00:14:47.767 --> 00:14:49.933
I don't know what
that's supposed to mean.

00:14:49.933 --> 00:14:51.567
Excuse us.

00:14:51.567 --> 00:14:54.700
But keep Takumi out of it.

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:57.333
He needs his rest more than anything.

00:14:57.333 --> 00:14:58.967
I understand.

00:14:58.967 --> 00:15:01.033
I'll escort him to the dormitory.

00:15:01.033 --> 00:15:02.967
Tate, you take Mai to the Headmaster.

00:15:02.967 --> 00:15:04.067
What?

00:15:06.567 --> 00:15:09.333
That Vice President guy sure is nice.

00:15:09.333 --> 00:15:11.100
He's like an understanding older brother.

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:16.600
Yeah, I guess.
A pretty amazing guy, for sure.

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:18.967
They say he and Council President Fujino

00:15:18.967 --> 00:15:20.900
are the most powerful couple
in the school's history.

00:15:20.900 --> 00:15:23.400
Huh? A couple?

00:15:27.933 --> 00:15:30.700
Pretty bad, huh.

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:34.933
I can't imagine lightning
doing that kind of damage.

00:15:34.933 --> 00:15:37.567
And then there was the ferry incident...

00:15:37.567 --> 00:15:39.933
There're a lot of weird things
going on these days.

00:15:39.933 --> 00:15:43.000
Hey! Maybe you're possessed
by a demon or something!

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:44.700
You saw?!

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:45.400
Huh?

00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:48.033
Uh, never mind...

00:15:48.033 --> 00:15:51.333
Then how about an exorcism?

00:15:51.333 --> 00:15:55.533
Seriously, I know a place
where they'll do it real cheap.

00:15:55.533 --> 00:15:57.500
Thanks, but no thanks!

00:15:57.500 --> 00:16:00.800
I thought you didn't want
anything to do with me!

00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:03.100
What're you freaking out about?

00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:04.467
Shut up!

00:16:04.467 --> 00:16:05.933
Out of my way!

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:11.067
I don't understand that girl.

00:16:11.067 --> 00:16:12.400
Hey, wait!

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:13.667
Wait up!

00:16:38.800 --> 00:16:41.467
We've been waiting for your arrival...

00:16:41.467 --> 00:16:42.867
...Mai Tokiha.

00:16:49.367 --> 00:16:50.567
You were at...

00:16:50.567 --> 00:16:51.767
Mai!

00:16:52.667 --> 00:16:54.033
Mai!

00:16:54.033 --> 00:16:55.533
Mikoto?!

00:16:59.467 --> 00:17:03.100
It seems that you two
are already getting along well.

00:17:03.100 --> 00:17:04.567
You're...

00:17:04.567 --> 00:17:08.567
The Headmaster of Fuka Academy,
Mashiro Kazahana.

00:17:08.567 --> 00:17:11.767
Welcome to Fuka Academy, Mai Tokiha.

00:17:13.533 --> 00:17:15.500
What?!

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:16.800
I see.

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:18.533
So that's what happened to your parents.

00:17:18.533 --> 00:17:23.033
I'm pretty sick all the time,
so I've been a huge burden to my sister.

00:17:23.033 --> 00:17:28.767
I was so happy that we got
scholarships to come here.

00:17:28.767 --> 00:17:32.067
Before we arrived, my sister and
I made a promise to each other.

00:17:32.067 --> 00:17:35.033
We promised to enjoy
school life to the fullest.

00:17:35.033 --> 00:17:37.400
Sounds like you have a great sister.

00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:38.800
Yup!

00:17:53.067 --> 00:17:56.867
Um, Miss Headmaster...

00:17:56.867 --> 00:17:58.433
Yes?

00:17:58.667 --> 00:18:04.567
I want to thank you for offering us
scholarships to attend this school.

00:18:04.567 --> 00:18:07.867
I hoped to come and thank you
as soon as we arrived...

00:18:07.867 --> 00:18:09.767
...but I got caught up in a few things...

00:18:09.767 --> 00:18:12.500
There's no need to thank me.

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:17.400
I did have an ulterior motive
in bringing you to this school.

00:18:18.100 --> 00:18:21.067
You're a HiME, like the others.

00:18:22.567 --> 00:18:25.567
That beast you girls fought last night...

00:18:25.567 --> 00:18:28.533
...is called an Orphan.

00:18:28.533 --> 00:18:30.033
Orphan?

00:18:30.033 --> 00:18:31.800
That's right.

00:18:31.800 --> 00:18:35.933
It's not from Earth.
It strayed from another world.

00:18:35.933 --> 00:18:37.733
The only ones that can fight them

00:18:37.733 --> 00:18:40.900
are maidens under
the guidance of a certain star.

00:18:42.467 --> 00:18:44.967
Only you HiME can fight them.

00:18:44.967 --> 00:18:47.433
That's why you called us here?

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:54.700
You called us here
in order to fight monsters?!

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:57.000
Yes.

00:18:57.000 --> 00:18:58.567
That's cruel.

00:18:58.567 --> 00:19:01.467
It's not fair! You tricked us!

00:19:01.467 --> 00:19:05.100
I'm responsible for someone
I promised to take care of.

00:19:05.100 --> 00:19:08.567
I don't have the time or energy
to deal with other people's problems!

00:19:08.567 --> 00:19:11.467
You mean your brother?

00:19:11.467 --> 00:19:14.567
If you'd like, I might be able to help...

00:19:16.700 --> 00:19:18.667
I'm terribly sorry.

00:19:18.667 --> 00:19:20.633
That was rude of me.

00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:31.433
Are you hungry, Mai?

00:19:31.433 --> 00:19:33.933
I think you're the hungry one.

00:19:38.333 --> 00:19:40.633
Why don't you go on
and take a bath first.

00:19:40.633 --> 00:19:42.467
And I'll make you something to eat.

00:19:42.467 --> 00:19:44.333
A bath?!

00:19:44.333 --> 00:19:45.867
No! Stop it!

00:19:45.867 --> 00:19:47.800
Just hold still!

00:19:47.800 --> 00:19:48.600
Stop!

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:51.000
--It's okay!
--No!

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:56.333
Don't know how to take a bath?!
Where did you come from?!

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:08.500
I won't force you to do this.

00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:12.767
And I won't take away
your scholarship, either.

00:20:12.767 --> 00:20:17.467
You must decide for yourself
what you would like to do.

00:20:19.367 --> 00:20:20.600
Hey, Mikoto...

00:20:20.600 --> 00:20:22.467
What are you going to do?

00:20:22.467 --> 00:20:25.633
Are you going to fight like she asked?

00:20:25.633 --> 00:20:27.833
I don't like the Headmaster.

00:20:27.833 --> 00:20:30.333
She is your legal guardian, you know.

00:20:30.333 --> 00:20:32.900
She covers all your school
and living expenses.

00:20:32.900 --> 00:20:35.033
I'm looking for my brother.

00:20:35.033 --> 00:20:37.333
And I'll fight anyone who gets in my way.

00:20:37.333 --> 00:20:38.633
End of story.

00:20:38.633 --> 00:20:40.800
Oh.

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:43.367
I wonder if I'll become like that...?

00:20:43.367 --> 00:20:45.467
My grandpa once told me...

00:20:45.467 --> 00:20:48.000
...that my brother is in the land of Fuka.

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:50.800
That's why I came here.

00:20:50.800 --> 00:20:53.667
Am I too much of a burden
staying with you?

00:20:53.667 --> 00:20:56.800
No, but what if you were?
Got anywhere else to go?

00:20:56.800 --> 00:20:58.067
No.

00:20:58.067 --> 00:21:00.400
It looks like we're stuck with each other.

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:02.533
Really...?

00:21:02.533 --> 00:21:05.533
Great. Thank goodness...

00:21:06.333 --> 00:21:07.433
Mikoto!

00:21:07.433 --> 00:21:09.367
Hey! Come on, Mikoto!

00:21:09.367 --> 00:21:10.900
You're so silly!

00:21:10.900 --> 00:21:12.733
Come on! Get it together!

00:21:12.733 --> 00:21:14.400
I feel dizzy...

00:21:14.400 --> 00:21:16.567
Come on!

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:30.367
All set.

00:21:34.633 --> 00:21:38.800
Wake up!

00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:40.500
Mikoto...

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:46.967
You look even better
than I thought you would.

00:21:46.967 --> 00:21:47.733
Here.

00:21:47.733 --> 00:21:48.833
Take it.

00:21:48.833 --> 00:21:49.967
It's your lunch.

00:21:49.967 --> 00:21:51.433
For you.

00:21:52.967 --> 00:21:55.700
Mai!

00:21:55.700 --> 00:21:57.467
Hey! Stop that!

00:21:59.467 --> 00:22:01.700
Oh! This is your roommate, Mai?

00:22:01.700 --> 00:22:04.533
Mikoto Minagi.

00:22:04.533 --> 00:22:06.033
You're in middle school, huh.

00:22:06.033 --> 00:22:06.967
What grade are you in?

00:22:06.967 --> 00:22:08.367
